  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nGenerally dry and breezy conditions will persist throughout \nmuch of the long-term period. Lingering moisture will allow for \na 15-30% chance of precipitation and a 15-20% chance of \nthunderstorms Wednesday afternoon, mainly near the ID/NV border \nand the Central ID Mountains. Beyond Wednesday, troughing off of\nthe west coast will push the moisture south and east of our \narea. Height falls throughout the period will allow for a slight\ncooling trend, with temperatures 2-7 degrees above normal \nthroughout the period. Uncertainty begins to increase late this \nweek, following the lifting of the initial trough and associated\nfrontal passage. However, cluster analysis is leaning towards \ntroughing digging back down into the weekend.",
